For each positive odd integer $m$, the sets
\begin{gather*}
\{a\in\mathbb{Z}_{\ge0}:m2^a\text{ is strongly pseudoperfect}\},\\
\{a\in\mathbb{Z}_{\ge0}:m2^a\text{ is extremely strongly pseudoperfect}\}
\end{gather*}
are ultimately periodic. For each set, an initial segment and a period
can be computed from the divisors of $m$.
